TYONG-WEB is my personal portfolio website, created to showcase who I am, the projects I've worked on, and the skills I've developed throughout my journey as a Computer Science student and aspiring Full-Stack Web Developer. It serves as a place where visitors can learn more about my background, explore the technologies I work with, and see how I apply what I've learned through academic and personal projects. More than just a collection of projects, this website reflects my growth, curiosity, and passion for building meaningful and user-friendly web applications.

The website was designed with simplicity and accessibility in mind, making it easy to navigate across both desktop and mobile devices. It includes sections that introduce me, highlight my technical skills, showcase my featured projects, and provide ways for visitors to connect with me. Every part of the website was planned to create a clean and organized experience while allowing my work and experiences to be presented in a clear and engaging way.

This project was built using HTML5, CSS3, and JavaScript, with each technology playing an important role in creating a responsive and interactive user experience. Git was used to manage version control during development, while GitHub hosts both the source code and the live website through GitHub Pages. Building this portfolio also gave me the opportunity to strengthen my understanding of responsive design, user interface development, and front-end best practices.

As I continue learning and taking on new projects, I plan to keep this portfolio updated with new work, improved features, and refinements that reflect my progress as a developer. My goal is for this website to grow alongside my skills and serve as an accurate representation of my experience, creativity, and commitment to continuous learning.
